      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# Polaris \u2014 Spine\n\nThe two stages of the main pipeline that resolve and enrich every event:\n\n```\nraw.events -> sync-identity-resolver -> identified.events -> sync-enrichment-runtime -> resolved.events\n```\n\n**Read the outcome panels first.** Both stages FAIL OPEN by design \u2014 a missing profile row, an over-size trait snapshot, an absent geo database and an event with no IP all produce a well-formed event with null-ish blocks. None of them raises the failure counter, so a silent degradation is invisible in throughput and error panels and visible only here.\n\n`merge_suspended` on the safeguards panel is the merge-rate breaker tripping: a profile absorbing more merges than policy allows inside its window. It is the signature of a promiscuous identifier (a kiosk device, `customer_id: \"guest\"`, a bot) chain-merging strangers into one person. Alert: `PolarisIdentityMergeBreakerTripped`.\n\n**The geo database panels are boot-time facts, not rates.** The stage reads the mmdb once at boot and holds that snapshot until it restarts, so both panels describe what each process LOADED \u2014 a refresh on disk moves neither of them until the pods cycle. `wired = 0` is the `geo:no_backend` outage stated without needing traffic to state it; a rising age is the failure nothing else here can show, because a stale database answers every lookup and hits on most of them. Alerts: `PolarisEnrichmentGeoipDatabaseMissing`, `PolarisEnrichmentGeoipDatabaseStale`; runbook: `docs/operations/runbook-geoip-refresh.md`.\n\nRunbooks: `docs/operations/runbook-processor-lag.md`, `docs/operations/runbook-spine-delivery-verification.md`."
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.4.0",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "text"
    },
